  "id": "COMPOUND:24149 - PROTEIN:5845",
  "verbalization": "Mexogenin appears to interact with SNU1 through a series of molecular pathways, with the microtubule-associated protein 1B acting as a central mediator. This protein is targeted by both Mexogenin and another compound, CID 11603911, which in turn targets SNU1. The presence of multiple targets—such as Sasanquasaponin I—suggests a complex network of interactions, potentially involving different pathways or mechanisms. The evidence points to a possible role of microtubule-associated proteins in mediating the effects of Mexogenin, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The integration of these targets highlights the importance of microtubule-associated proteins in the biological response to Mexogenin, though further investigation is needed to elucidate the precise molecular interactions.",
